      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe English Cookery Book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 edited by JH Walsh \u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#walsh-1859\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EWalsh 1859\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EFig Pudding.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n877. Add to one quarter of a pound of grated bread crumbs five and a half ounces of finely chopped suet, and about six ounces of moist sugar, then beat two eggs and put them to the above, adding just enough of cold milk to make the pudding of a proper consistency. Boil it full four hours, and, if approved, it may be served with \u003Ca href=\u0022wine-sauce.html\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Ewine sauce\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E.\u003Cbr\u003E"
